From 0002-pra-emmc-dma Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PRA eMMC 0002 v3] SDMA for the per-sector CMD17 path behind
 emmcdma=1 (default off), runtime-verified; caps2 print; rebased onto 0164

DRAFT - not applied, not committed. v3 REBASES v2 onto the 0164 driver
state: verified with the 0164 method (GNU patch -p1 --fuzz=0 on the
index-stripped diff against the reconstructed CI-built tree: pristine
xnu-8796.141.3 + stack 0001..0165 with pre-skips 0031/0041/0097/0099/0127/
0129). The 0164 content is the intended 0163 driver (per-sector CMD17
default, pra_emmc_multi_ok defaults false, busy_note()/recover(), the
CMD23 block, the ladder), so v2's hunks carried over; what changed:

1. VERIFICATION METHOD: v2 was verified with `git apply` on the xnu-src
   stacked tree - exactly the method section 14 of the WORKLOG discredited
   (git 2.56 skip-detects already-applied hunks with rc=0). v3 is verified
   with GNU patch --fuzz=0 on the reconstructed tree, both against the
   plain 0164+0165 state AND stacked after drafts 0003+0004+0005+0006
   (transcripts in WORKLOG section 15.1; both orders byte-identical).

2. TWO blocks moved so 0002 applies in ANY landing order relative to
   drafts 0003-0006 (verified both ways, transcripts in WORKLOG 15.1):
   - the map_host emmcdma parse block moved BEFORE the emmcmulti block
     (was: after it, right before `return 0`), because 0005 (emmctest
     parse) and 0006 (milestone print) append at the tail of map_host;
   - the SDMA state block (dma_ok/dma_phys/externs/recover forward decl)
     moved AFTER the stats block (was: between pra_emmc_multi_buf and
     pra_emmc_stats), because 0003 and 0005 insert their statics in that
     exact gap. NOTE: GNU patch 2.8.1 needs >=3 trailing context lines
     (or EOF) to match a hunk at --fuzz=0 - hand-trimmed 1-line-context
     hunks fail even when byte-exact (found and recorded in WORKLOG
     15.1), so adjacency conflicts are resolved by moving insertion
     points, never by trimming context.
   Parse/declaration order is irrelevant - the flags are independent.

3. Banner text updated (0163/commit-ecfdc55 references -> the 0164 state
   and the reconstruction recipe).

EVERYTHING ELSE IS v2's CONTENT, UNCHANGED:

- SDMA applies to the CMD17 PER-SECTOR path - the default path since
  0164 - replacing the 128 32-bit buffer-port reads with one controller
  DMA into the 64 KiB bounce buffer plus a 512-byte memcpy. Per SDHCI
  3.0 the SDMA System Address register is 0x00, its own register
  (Argument is 0x08), written BEFORE the command with the transfer-mode
  DMA-enable bit set; the old v1 "0x08 after the command" latch trick was
  a spec misreading and is gone. Everything stays polled: transfer
  complete from NORMAL_INT_STATUS, no interrupts.
- Opt-in emmcdma=1, default OFF - the default boot is byte-identical to
  the proven PIO path. At probe: the 64 KiB bounce must be physically
  contiguous page by page (ml_vtophys 4 KiB walk), 4-byte aligned, below
  4 GiB - otherwise ONE "emmcdma=1 rejected" line and PIO for the boot.
  Host-control bit 3 forced to 0 = SDMA (LK handoff 0x800bf4 already
  clear, ring19:2), old+new printed. Any DMA data-phase failure (error
  bits or 2M-iteration timeout) prints ONE line, runs pra_emmc_recover()
  and latches pra_emmc_dma_ok off for the boot; the caller finishes that
  request PIO.
- Bounce-buffer target, not the caller's page: a misfire corrupts a known
  static buffer, and the probe-time contiguity proof over the whole 64
  KiB carries to the future emmcdma=2 chunk mode.
- caps2 (0x44) printed at probe (bits 0/1/2 = SDR50/SDR104/DDR50, bit 3
  HS200) and acted on not at all; it had never been read before this
  series.
- Write path untouched (CMD24 stays PIO).

WHAT THE STATS WILL SHOW (emmcdma=1, emmcstats=1): wait stays ~137-145 us
(entry to TRANSFER COMPLETE - the ~137 us command overhead is still
inside it, SDMA cannot remove that), buf collapses ~42 us -> ~1-2 us (the
memcpy). Per-sector ceiling moves ~2.7 -> ~3.5 MB/s. That ceiling is the
point: it proves the port drain is gone and only command overhead is
left. The real speedup requires the CMD23 chunk path (emmcmulti=1, the
next experiment boot, WORKLOG section 13) or the emmcdma=2 follow-up
(flag named and rejected-with-a-print here).

UNKNOWN (why default off, why one-strike latch): whether this Arasan
honours the DMA-enable bit and the 0x00 system address at LK handoff;
vendor register needs. A wrong guess costs ONE sector read: one print,
one recover, PIO for the rest of the boot - the containment shape 0164
gives the CMD23 experiment.

VERIFY: GNU `patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --dry-run` against the reconstructed
tree (WORKLOG section 15.1 transcripts). Do NOT trust `git apply --check`
(git 2.56 skip-detects, rc=0).
